Subject: WPE: Phoenix build configuration: OpenSSL digests, static libWPEWebKit, multi-call program hook

WPE hard-requires libgcrypt and libtasn1 even with ENABLE_WEB_CRYPTO=OFF; then PAL's SHA
digests are their only users. On Phoenix use OpenSSL (already linked for glib-networking):
USE_OPENSSL instead of USE_GCRYPT, PAL's CryptoDigestOpenSSL.cpp, and WebCore's OpenSSL WebCrypto
sources when ENABLE_WEB_CRYPTO is on. libWPEWebKit is STATIC (no shared libraries; CMake would turn
SHARED into STATIC on its own, but WebKit's sub-target objects only reach a shared link).
PHOENIX_BROWSER_DIR adds the out-of-tree multi-call program (tools/browser/wpe/launcher).

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 981edf67988dda94c6456615a3fb982b0f8cc8c8..2c1ca510c4c6364ad06a9ad57bea126618e776d1 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -74,6 +74,12 @@ endif ()
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 add_subdirectory(Source)
 
+# Phoenix-RTOS: the static multi-call browser program (UI + WebProcess + NetworkProcess in
+# one ELF), kept outside this tree (coordination repo tools/browser/wpe/launcher).
+if (PHOENIX_BROWSER_DIR)
+    add_subdirectory(${PHOENIX_BROWSER_DIR} ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/PhoenixBrowser)
+endif ()
+
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Add tools
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
